# Goal: Build Module 17 (Knowledge Base & RAG Document Search)

This is the "Wow-Factor" module of your FYP. We will build the system that allows your business owners to upload their internal documents (PDFs, Text files), which we will process, split into chunks, embed using AI, and store in a Vector Database so their Chatbots can perform semantic search.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend Data Modeling (`backend/models.py`)
- **[NEW]** Create a `Document` model to track the files:
  - `id`, `tenant_id` (ForeignKey)
  - `name` (e.g., "Company_Handbook.pdf")
  - `file_type` (e.g., "PDF")
  - `size` (Integer in bytes)
  - `status` (e.g., "Completed", "Processing", "Failed")
  - `embeddings_count` (Integer)
  - `created_at`

### 2. New AI Dependencies (`backend/requirements.txt`)
- **[MODIFY]** Add standard RAG libraries: `python-multipart` (for file uploads), `langchain`, `langchain-huggingface`, `pypdf`, and `faiss-cpu`. 
*(Note: I am substituting Qdrant with FAISS because FAISS can be installed directly via Python without needing to configure Docker! This makes your FYP much easier to run and demo).*

### 3. Backend Schemas & Router (`backend/routers/documents.py`)
- **[NEW]** Router `documents.py` with endpoints:
  - `GET /api/documents`: Fetch all documents for the current tenant.
  - `POST /api/documents/upload`: Accepts `multipart/form-data`. Saves the file, reads the PDF text, splits it into chunks using LangChain, generates embeddings using a lightweight open-source HuggingFace model, and saves it to a local FAISS index!
  - `DELETE /api/documents/{id}`: Deletes the document.

### 4. Frontend Integration
- **[MODIFY]** `KnowledgeBasePage.tsx`: Fetch and display real documents from the DB instead of mock data.
- **[MODIFY]** `UploadDocumentsPage.tsx`: Wire up the File dropzone to actually send the selected files to the FastAPI backend using `FormData`.

